{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Power_Through","to":"Power Through"},{"from":"Noxious_Fumes","to":"Noxious Fumes"},{"from":"Biased_Cognition","to":"Biased Cognition"},{"from":"Talk_to_the_Hand","to":"Talk to the Hand"},{"from":"Reckless_Charge","to":"Reckless Charge"},{"from":"Through_Violence","to":"Through Violence"},{"from":"Glass_Knife","to":"Glass Knife"},{"from":"Rip_and_Tear","to":"Rip and Tear"}],"pages":{"2088":{"pageid":2088,"ns":0,"title":"Biased Cognition","revisions":[{"revid":56897,"parentid":56896,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Biased Cognition\n|Image       = Blue-BiasedCognition.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (4;5) {{BD|Focus}}.<br>At the start of your turn, lose 1 {{BD|Focus}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Bias, Focus\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Bias\n|Image        = Icon Bias.png\n|Description  = At the start of your turn, lose X {{BD|Focus}}.\n|Type         = Debuff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n|GivesToPlayer = Focus (Negative)\n}}\n{{C|Biased Cognition}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}. <!---When played, it applies 4 (5) {{BD|Focus}}, as well as the {{BD|Bias}} {{KW|Debuff}}, which removes 1 {{BD|Focus}} at the start of each of your turns.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Bias}} removes {{BD|Focus}} ''after'' the additional [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] from {{C|Loop}} and {{R|Emotion Chip}} happen, despite the numbers on the Orbs changing visually first.\n* If an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} and a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} have already been played this turn, playing Biased Cognition may trigger {{R|Orange Pellets}}. If it does, {{BD|Bias}} will be cleared immediately.\n* In general, additive effects are applied before multiplicative ones. If a damaging Orb is improved by {{BD|Focus}} and then damages an enemy with {{BD|Lock-On}}, the {{BD|Focus}} will be added before the 50% increase from {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Like all sources of {{BD|Focus}}, Biased Cognition improves the output of {{KW|Lightning}}, {{KW|Frost}}, and {{KW|Dark}} Orbs.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} stack, so Biased Cognition also works well with {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, and {{R|Data Disk}}.\n* {{BD|Bias}} is a [[Debuff]], and can be prevented with sources of {{BD|Artifact}} such as {{C|Core Surge}}, as well as removed by {{R|Orange Pellets}}.\n** Note that the {{BD|Artifact}} has to be applied ''before'' Biased Cognition is played. Otherwise, the {{BD|Artifact}} will only consume the first removal of {{BD|Focus}}, if anything.\n** On the other hand, {{R|Orange Pellets}} has to happen ''after'' the {{BD|Bias}} is applied, but this can be triggered by playing Biased Cognition itself. If {{R|Orange Pellets}} is activated on a subsequent turn, {{BD|Bias}} will still be cleared, but any {{BD|Focus}} lost in the interrim is not restored (unless you have negative {{BD|Focus}}).\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy, and applies after {{BD|Focus}} for large damage output.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Stacking {{BD|Bias}} will result in losing multiple {{BD|Focus}} per turn.\n* {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} are wholly unaffected by {{BD|Focus}}.\n* At first glance, it appears Biased Cognition will break even after 4 (5) turns. However, the value gained from {{BD|Focus}} in the meantime makes it take longer than that. Consider a simple example where you only have a single {{KW|Lightning}} Orb. If you play Biased Cogntition, it will deal 7 damage, then 6, then 5, etc. After 7 turns, you will have dealt 28 damage with Biased Cognition, and your {{BD|Focus}} will now be 0. On the other hand, if you hadn't played it, you'd deal 3 damage every turn, for a total of just 21 damage after 7 turns, and would still require another 3 turns to surpass the former example.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, undoing the benefit of Biased Cognition. However, as Biased Cognition will eventually remove all of its own {{BD|Focus}} anyway, {{C|Hyperbeam}} can still be useful as a finisher.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2086":{"pageid":2086,"ns":0,"title":"Consume","revisions":[{"revid":56947,"parentid":55705,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Consume\n|Image       = Blue-Consume.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (2;3) {{BD|Focus}}.<br>Lose 1 {{KW|Orb Slot}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Focus, Orb Slot\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Focus}} {{Keyword_Infobox|Orb Slot}}\n{{C|Consume}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}. <!---Consume removes your left-most Orb Slot, in return for 2 (3) {{BD|Focus}}. If the Orb Slot currently has an Orb in it, the Orb is removed, without {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} anything.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* In general, additive effects are applied before multiplicative ones. If a damaging Orb is improved by {{BD|Focus}} and then damages an enemy with {{BD|Lock-On}}, the {{BD|Focus}} will be added before the 50% increase from {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Like all sources of {{BD|Focus}}, Consume improves the output of {{KW|Lightning}}, {{KW|Frost}}, and {{KW|Dark}} Orbs.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} stack, so Consume also works well with {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, and {{R|Data Disk}}.\n* As {{BD|Focus}} becomes useless without Orb Slots, Consume can normally only be played up to twice. Sources of additional Orb Slots can improve this: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}.\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy, and applies after {{BD|Focus}} for large damage output.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Consume will always remove the left-most Orb Slot. If there is an Orb in the slot when it is removed, the Orb is removed, and nothing is {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}.\n* If all of your Orb Slots are removed, attempting to {{KW|Channel}} or {{KW|Evoke}} Orbs will have no effect.\n* If Consume is played while you have no Orb Slots, you will still gain {{BD|Focus}}, but it will not be useful unless you can gain more slots somehow.\n* The Orb Slot reduction is not a [[Debuff]], and cannot be prevented with {{BD|Artifact}} or undone via {{R|Orange Pellets}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Barrage}}, {{C|Fission}}, and {{C|Compile Driver}} all benefit from having additional Orb Slots.\n* {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} are wholly unaffected by {{BD|Focus}}, so the loss of Orb Slots is purely a downside for them.\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, undoing the benefit of Consume.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2304":{"pageid":2304,"ns":0,"title":"Devotion","revisions":[{"revid":55739,"parentid":50700,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Devotion\n|Image       = Purple-Devotion.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = At the start of your turn, gain (2;3) {{BD|Mantra}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Devotion}}{{Power Infobox|Mantra}}{{C|Devotion}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Devotion}}, which gives that amount of {{BD|Mantra}} at the start of every turn. When reaching 10 {{BD|Mantra}}, all of it will be removed and you will enter the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Brilliance}} increases in damage whenever you gain {{BD|Mantra}}.\n\n* All {{BD|Mantra}} sources synergize with eachother: {{C|Prostrate}},{{C|Pray}}, {{C|Worship}} and {{R|Damaru}} work well with {{C|Devotion}}.\n\n* When entering {{KW|Divinity}} if you are not in {{KW|Divinity}} yet, you will gain 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' and switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* While in {{KW|Divinity}}, all damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} is tripled. This does not affect damage from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2442":{"pageid":2442,"ns":0,"title":"Discovery","revisions":[{"revid":55416,"parentid":50722,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Discovery\n|Image       = Colorless-Discovery.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Choose 1 of 3 random cards to add into your hand. It costs 0 this turn.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Discovery}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It will generate a random card, which will have its normal cost replaced by 0 for this turn. {{C|Discovery}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself, if it is not upgraded. X-cost cards generated this way will still consume all your energy. \n\n== Obtaining Discovery ==\n{{C|Discovery}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Some cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n==== Cards with permanent effects ====\n* {{C|Feed}}, {{C|Reaper}}\n* {{C|Alchemize}}\n* {{C|Self Repair}}\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}}, {{C|Wish}}\n* {{C|Bandage Up}}, {{C|Bite}}\n==== b) Cards with exclusive sources ====\n* {{C|Apparition}}, {{C|J.A.X.}},  {{C|Ritual Dagger}} \n* {{C|Shiv}}\n* {{C|Beta}}, {{C|Insight}}, {{C|Miracle}}, {{C|Omega}}, {{C|Safety}}, {{C|Smite}}, {{C|Through Violence}}\n\n== Notes ==\n{{C|Discovery}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 55: Blur'''\n** Draw, Discard, and Exhaust piles can now be viewed during Codex/Discovery card selection.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like  Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 43: Discovery'''\n** Can no longer skip cards when choosing a card via Discovery.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Discovery.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2102":{"pageid":2102,"ns":0,"title":"Fusion","revisions":[{"revid":55797,"parentid":50590,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Fusion\n|Image       = Blue-Fusion.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|CostPlus    = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Plasma}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}} {{Keyword Infobox|Plasma}}\n{{C|Fusion}} is a 2 (1) {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}. <!---It {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 1 {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orb}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* The {{Icon|BE}} Energy generated by Fusion's {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orb}} allows for playing expensive and X cost cards, such as {{C|Echo Form}}, {{C|Meteor Strike}}, {{C|Tempest}}, {{C|Reinforced Body}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}}.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} more frequently.\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{BD|Focus}} has no effect on {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}}, {{C|Consume}} removing an Orb Slot is a strict downside for {{KW|Plasma}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The artwork for Fusion appears to depict a {{KW|Plasma}} Orb being formed by combining {{KW|Lightning}}, {{KW|Frost}}, and {{KW|Dark}} Orbs.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Fusion card works better for modders now\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2033":{"pageid":2033,"ns":0,"title":"Glass Knife","revisions":[{"revid":55802,"parentid":50536,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Glass Knife\n|Image       = Green-GlassKnife.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (8;12) damage twice. Decrease the damage of this card by 2 this combat.\n}}\n{{C|Glass Knife}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits 2 times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 24: Potions?!'''\n** Glass Knife card description: \"Glass Knife's damage\" -> \"This card's damage\"\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Glass Knife card buff.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2120":{"pageid":2120,"ns":0,"title":"Hyperbeam","revisions":[{"revid":55820,"parentid":50622,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Hyperbeam\n|Image       = Blue-Hyperbeam.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (26;34) damage to ALL enemies.<br>Lose 3 {{BD|Focus}}.\n}}\n{{C|Hyperbeam}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. <!--It does 26 (34) damage to ALL enemies, and removes 3 {{BD|Focus}}.-->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies === \n* Once you start lowering {{BD|Focus}}, doing so more is generally much less of a downside, so Hyperbeam and {{C|Reprogram}} work well together.\n* {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} do not benefit from {{BD|Focus}}, and are unaffected by its removal: {{C|Fusion}}, {{C|Meteor Strike}}, {{R|Nuclear Battery}}\n** {{C|Chaos}} can also produce {{KW|Plasma}}, but is much more likely to produce Orbs affected by the {{BD|Focus}} loss.\n\n* {{C|Core Surge}}, {{C|Panacea}}, {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}}, and {{R|Orange Pellets}} may all be used to prevent/remove the {{BD|Focus}} loss of Hyperbeam, allowing it to be used without affecting your Orbs.\n** Note that {{R|Orange Pellets}} can only clear negative {{BD|Focus}}, and it will not fix Hyperbeam taking away positive {{BD|Focus}}.\n\n* If a character other than [[The Defect]] manages to get Hyperbeam, such as from {{R|Prismatic Shard}}, the downside is essentially eliminated.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Focus}} only affects the future growth of {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}}, minimizing the effect of Hyperbeam on them later in combats.\n** In particular, since {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} target the enemy with the lowest current HP, Hyperbeam can be used to clear out lower HP enemies so your {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} can hit the bigger targets.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Hyperbeam reduces the effectiveness of sources that add {{BD|Focus}}: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Hyperbeam also weakens all non-{{KW|Plasma}} Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}.\n** As a secondary effect of this, many Orb-related cards do not work well with Hyperbeam, such as {{C|Compile Driver}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Hyperbeam card buff: 25 -> 26 damage. Upgraded: 32 -> 34.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1847":{"pageid":1847,"ns":0,"title":"Juggernaut","revisions":[{"revid":56612,"parentid":56395,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Juggernaut\n| Image       = Red-Juggernaut.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Whenever you gain {{KW|Block}}, deal (5;7) damage to a random enemy.\n| PowerGives = Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Juggernaut\n| Image        = Icon Juggernaut.png\n| Description  = Whenever you gain {{KW|Block}}, deal X damage to a random enemy.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| InteractsWith = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Juggernaut}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It grants 5 (7 if upgraded) {{BD|Juggernaut}}, which deals damage equal to that amount whenever you gain {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with any source of block, but particularly with block that can activate multiple times, such as {{C|Rage}}, {{C|Second Wind}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{R|Ornamental Fan}} or {{R|The Abacus}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Juggernaut will only be triggered by gaining separate instances of {{KW|Block}}. This means that {{BD|Metallicize}}, {{BD|Plated Armor}} and {{BD|Next Turn Block}} will only trigger it only once each regardless of how many different sources they have.\n** For example, playing two {{C|Metallicize}} cards will still result in only one trigger of {{BD|Juggernaut}} per turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Juggernaut damage not changing targets if original target is dead.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** Tingsha, Sword Boomerang, Bouncing Flask, Rip and Tear, Thunder Orbs, Havoc, and Juggernaut now utilize seeded enemy target randomization.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Juggernaut power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Juggernaut+ card buff: Upgrade amount 1 -> 2.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Juggernaut card buff: Damage 3 -> 5. Upgraded 5 -> 6.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Juggernaut was not working properly. Fixed.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Juggernaut card nerf.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Juggernaut's description gets simpler.\n** Juggernaut power's value is now colored blue.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2209":{"pageid":2209,"ns":0,"title":"Melter","revisions":[{"revid":50597,"parentid":36250,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Melter\n|Image       = Blue-Melter.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Remove all {{KW|Block}} from the enemy.<br>Deal (10;14) damage.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}{{C|Melter}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It removes all {{KW|Block}} from the target and then deals 10 (14 if upgraded) damage.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* It first removes {{KW|Block}} from the target and only then deals damage, meaning its damage directly translates into HP lost by the target.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Many enemies have ways to gain {{KW|Block}}, but not all, and not in all combats or turns. This means that relatively often, {{C|Melter}} is nothing more than a simple damage card.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Melter}} will not trigger {{R|Hand Drill}} as it does not ''break'' the enemy's {{KW|Block}} but instead ''removes it'' entirely.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The art depicts a molten {{M|Spheric Guardian}}, an enemy against which {{C|Melter}} is notably useful.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1966":{"pageid":1966,"ns":0,"title":"Noxious Fumes","revisions":[{"revid":56787,"parentid":56786,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Noxious Fumes\n| Image       = Green-NoxiousFumes.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = At the start of your turn, apply (2;3) {{BD|Poison}} to ALL enemies.\n| PowerGives = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Noxious Fumes\n| Image        = Icon NoxiousFumes.png\n| Description  = At the start of your turn, apply X {{BD|Poison}} to ALL enemies.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToEnemy = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}\n{{C|Noxious Fumes}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\nAs {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy's turn, it has some unusual interactions:\n* If the damage is enough to cause {{M|The Guardian}} to change to Defensive form, it will immediately change its [[Intent]] to apply {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Moreover, as it is already past the point in its turn where {{KW|Block}} is removed, it will keep the Block generated by moving to Defensive Form until its next turn.\n** Notably, in other cases where HP thresholds affect enemy [[Intent]] (such as {{M|The Champ}} and {{M|Time Eater}}), this happens on a subsequent turn, and will not be affected.\n* If the enemy dies to {{BD|Poison}}, the card drawn by {{R|Gremlin Horn}} will be held until your next turn.\n** Similarly, if a {{M|Bronze Orb}} dies while holding a card in Stasis, that card will be returned to you and stay in your hand until next turn.\n* If a {{M|Fungi Beast}} dies this way, you will receive {{BD|Vulnerable}} during the enemy turn, which may increase the amount of incoming damage for the turn.\n* If an enemy with {{BD|Minion|Minions}} dies this way, its Minions will still flee combat before attacking.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Bane}} does additional damage if the target has {{BD|Poison}}.\n* {{C|Catalyst}} can double (triple) the amount of {{BD|Poison}} on a target.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} can be used in combats with multiple enemies to consolidate {{BD|Poison}} as enemies die.\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} applies 1 {{BD|Poison}} whenever this card applies {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n* {{C|Noxious Fumes}} works well with other sources of {{BD|Poison}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}, {{C|Envenom}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}}.\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Poison}} damage causes {{M|Lagavulin}} to wake up, consuming its Stunned turn in the process.\n* {{BD|Poison}} bypasses {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Flying}}.\n* However, {{BD|Intangible}} reduces ''all'' sources of HP loss to 1, including {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will prevent applying {{BD|Poison}}. {{BD|Noxious Fumes}} will naturally clear out {{BD|Artifact}} over time.\n* Certain bosses will remove all [[Debuffs]] during combat: {{M|The Champ}}, {{M|Awakened One}}, and {{M|Time Eater}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Noxious Fumes power.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1812":{"pageid":1812,"ns":0,"title":"Panache","revisions":[{"revid":55885,"parentid":50746,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Panache\n|Image       = Colorless-Panache.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Every time you play 5 cards in a single turn, deal (10;14) damage to ALL enemies.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Panache}}\n{{C|Panache}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It applies the {{BD|Panache}} effect on the player, which does 10 (14) damage to ALL enemies every time you play 5 cards in one turn. This effect can trigger more than once per turn, so for instance playing 10 cards in one turn will cause the damage to occur twice.\n\n== Obtaining Panache ==\n{{C|Panache}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\nRegardless of character, there exist ways to play infinite cards in a single turn, which naturally synergizes with Panache. As there are many different ways to go infinite, and most infinites generate damage even without Panache, for the rest of this section only finite strategies are listed.\n\n==== a) As the Ironclad ====\n[[Ironclad]] usually does not play very many cards in a turn, and so will rarely be able to proc Panache. \n* {{C|Corruption}} makes all Skills cost 0, allowing more cards to be played most turns.\n* {{C|Offering}} and {{C|Seeing Red}} both generate {{Icon|RE}}, and may allow playing more cards in a turn.\n\n==== b) As the Silent ====\n[[Silent]] tends to play many cards at once fairly easily, and generally benefits the most from Panache.\n* {{C|Shiv}} generation cards, especially {{C|Blade Dance}} and {{C|Storm of Steel}}, enable playing 5 cards for very little {{Icon|GE}}.\n* {{C|Adrenaline}}, {{C|Concentrate}}, {{C|Outmaneuver}}, {{C|Flying Knee}} and {{C|Tactician}} all give you access to more Energy.\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} makes your whole hand cost 0 temporarily.\n* {{C|Choke}} does not directly enable more card plays, but it also benefits from many cards being played at once.\n\n==== c) As the Defect ====\n[[Defect]] primarily benefits from Panache when either using a 0-cost strategy or [[Orbs#Plasma Orbs|Plasma Orbs]].\n* {{C|All for One}} and {{C|Scrape}} enable playing lots of 0 cost cards in a single turn.\n* Sources of Plasma allow you to consistently have more {{Icon|BE}} each turn: {{C|Fusion}}, {{C|Meteor Strike}}, {{C|Chaos}}, and {{R|Nuclear Battery}}.\n* Defect also has various other Energy generation methods: {{C|Double Energy}}, {{C|Aggregate}}, {{C|Fission}}, {{C|Recycle}}, and {{C|TURBO}}.\n\n==== d) As the Watcher ====\n[[Watcher]] has quite a lot of ways to generate both cards that cost 0 and {{Icon|PE}} (thanks in part to both [[Keywords#Stance|Calm]] and [[Keywords#Stance|Divinity]]).\n* Sources of {{C|Miracle}}s: {{C|Collect}}, {{C|Deus Ex Machina}}, and {{R|Pure Water}}.\n* Sources of {{KW|Scry}} allow you to manipulate your hand, avoiding drawing dead cards: {{C|Third Eye}}, {{C|Foresight}}, and {{C|Cut Through Fate}}.\n* {{C|Scrawl}} gives you access to many cards at once.\n* {{C|Deva Form}} gives you a huge amount of Energy as combat goes on, enabling lots of card plays per turn consistently.\n\n==== e) All Classes ====\n* {{C|Enlightenment}} and {{C|Madness}} both reduce the cost of cards potentially allowing playing more cards per turn.\n* {{C|Purity}} allows you to exhaust several cards at will, allowing the removal of {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}} or unwanted cards like {{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strike}}, allowing you to draw cheap cards more consistently.\n\n==== f) Relics ====\n* Any relic which gives Energy.\n* {{R|Unceasing Top}} allows you to continuously draw more cards to play, assuming you have energy left.\n* {{R|Mummified Hand}} makes cards temporarily free when playing Powers.\n* Various relics benefit from playing lots of cards as well: {{R|Ornamental Fan}}, {{R|Letter Opener}}, {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n\n==== a) Strength ====\nIs completely unaffected by {{BD|Strength}}. This means the debuff from [[Spire Spear]] will have no effect on it, but neither will {{R|Shuriken}}, {{R|Vajra}}, or {{C|Inflame}}.\n\n==== b) Thorns and Flight ====\nAs Panache does not do Attack damage, it bypasses [[Shapes#Spiker|Spikers]]' {{BD|Thorns}} and [[Byrd|Byrds]]' {{BD|Flying}}, but it also does not benefit from [[Giant Head]]'s {{BD|Slow}}.\n\n==== c) Stances ====\nSimilarly, the damage from Panache is not affected by being in [[Keywords#Stance|Wrath]] or [[Keywords#Stance|Divinity]]. However, the Energy generated by entering Divinity may make it easier to proc the damage in the first place.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1932":{"pageid":1932,"ns":0,"title":"Power Through","revisions":[{"revid":56757,"parentid":50793,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Rename|Power Through|Fight Through}} {{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Power Through\n| Image       = Red-PowerThrough.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Add 2 {{C|Wound|Wounds}} into your hand.<br>Gain (15;20) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Small Card Infobox|Wound}}\n{{C|Power Through}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 15 (20 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and adds 2 {{C|Wound|Wounds}} into your hand.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Power Through}} is one of the few cards that increases the amount of cards in hand without drawing from your own deck, and therefore synergizes with {{C|Second Wind}} and {{C|Fiend Fire}}, as well as any other card that requires fodder to {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n\n* Synergizes with {{C|Fire Breathing}} and {{C|Evolve}}, as it creates {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} cards. However, the {{C|Wound|Wounds}} get created in your hand, meaning it can take some time before they can be drawn to trigger these effects.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{C|Wound}} generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1860":{"pageid":1860,"ns":0,"title":"Reckless Charge","revisions":[{"revid":50440,"parentid":35967,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Reckless Charge\n|Image       = Red-RecklessCharge.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (7;10) damage.<br>Shuffle a {{C|Dazed}} into your draw pile.\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Dazed}}\n{{C|Reckless Charge}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage and adds a {{C|Dazed}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order === \n* The {{C|Dazed}} gets added into your draw pile ''before'' triggering {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with {{C|Fire Breathing}} and {{C|Evolve}}, as it creates a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card in your draw pile.\n\n* The {{C|Dazed}} generated by this can be used as a part of {{KW|Exhaust}} synergy, especially in combination with {{R|Medical Kit}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Reckless Charge card is now Uncommon.\n** Reckless Charge+ card nerfed damage by 1.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 20: Immolate'''\n** Reckless charge is now Common and shuffles a Dazed into your draw pile rather than making you Vulnerable.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2258":{"pageid":2258,"ns":0,"title":"Rip and Tear","revisions":[{"revid":55924,"parentid":50602,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Rip and Tear\n|Image       = Blue-RipandTear.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;9) damage to a random enemy twice.\n}}\n{{C|Rip and Tear}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (9 if upgraded) damage twice, each time to a random enemy.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits two times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Rip and Tear, Sword Boomerang, and Thunder Strike continuing its hits over Thorns and Shifting powers.\n** Fixed Wrist Blade not affecting Sword Boomerang, Rip and Tear, and Thunder Strike.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** Tingsha, Sword Boomerang, Bouncing Flask, Rip and Tear, Thunder Orbs, Havoc, and Juggernaut now utilize seeded enemy target randomization.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Rip and Tear card gets VFX.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1799":{"pageid":1799,"ns":0,"title":"Shiv","revisions":[{"revid":56365,"parentid":55497,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Shiv\n| Image       = Colorless-Shiv.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Special\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Deal (4;6) damage.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Shiv}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 (6 if upgraded) damage and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} when played. \n\n== Creating Shivs == \n{{C|Shiv}} cannot be added to the player's deck, and can only be created in combat. {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} can only be created using the following means:\n\n====Cards ==== \n\n* {{C|Blade Dance}}\n* {{C|Cloak and Dagger}}\n* {{C|Storm of Steel}}\n* {{C|Infinite Blades}}\n\n====Relics ==== \n\n* {{R|Ninja Scroll}} \n\n==== c) Potions ====\n\n* {{P|Cunning Potion}} (creates upgraded {{C|Shiv|Shivs}})\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Accuracy}} will increase the damage of every {{C|Shiv}} by 4, or 6 if {{C|Accuracy}} is upgraded. Playing additional copies of {{C|Accuracy}} will continue adding to {{C|Shiv}} damage.\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of each {{C|Shiv}} by 4.\n* Having {{C|Master Reality}} in play before creating a {{C|Shiv}} will create an upgraded {{C|Shiv}} instead.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Accuracy power now correctly works with Shivs played from the top of the deck via cards like Mayhem or Havoc.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Shiv and J.A.X can no longer spawn from effects like Jack Of All Trades and Transmutation.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Accuracy wasn't working with Shiv+\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Shiv+. +2 damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Fixed a case where Shiv would not be marked as seen in the Card Library.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2075":{"pageid":2075,"ns":0,"title":"Stack","revisions":[{"revid":50567,"parentid":36223,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Stack\n|Image       = Blue-Stack.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain {{KW|Block}} equal to the number of cards in your discard pile(;+3).\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Stack}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* A played {{C|Stack}} card will give {{KW|Block}} before it is put in the discard pile, and therefore will not count itself when giving block.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2297":{"pageid":2297,"ns":0,"title":"Study","revisions":[{"revid":55963,"parentid":50682,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Study\n|Image       = Purple-Study.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|CostPlus    = 1\n|Description = At the end of your turn, shuffle an {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Study}} {{Small Card Infobox|Insight}}\n{{C|Study}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives one {{BD|Study}}, which shuffles an {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile at the end of every turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Starting from the moment you play {{C|Master Reality}}, it will shuffle upgraded {{C|Insight|Insights}} into your draw pile instead.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Insight}} has no effect on its own except for cycling through cards, it is not benefitial when there is a restriction or downside to playing ({{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}) cards, such as with {{BD|Time Warp}}, {{BD|Hex}}, {{BD|Beat of Death}} or {{R|Velvet Choker}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2299":{"pageid":2299,"ns":0,"title":"Talk to the Hand","revisions":[{"revid":55969,"parentid":55507,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Talk to the Hand\n|Image       = Purple-TalktotheHand.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (5;7) damage. Whenever you attack this enemy, gain (2;3) {{KW|Block}}. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Block Return}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Talk to the Hand}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (7 if upgraded) damage and applies 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Block Return}}, after which it {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* It first deals damage and then applies {{BD|Block Return}}, meaning it will not yet benefit from the {{BD|Block Return}} it just applied.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Block Return}} activates per hit, meaning it synergizes with {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} that hit multiple times, notably:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Flying Sleeves}}, {{C|Tantrum}} and {{C|Ragnarok}}.\n* {{C|Expunger}} from a {{C|Conjure Blade}} played with X (or X+1 if upgraded) larger than 1.\n* {{C|Bowling Bash}} if more than 1 enemy is present.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|Block Return}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2314":{"pageid":2314,"ns":0,"title":"Through Violence","revisions":[{"revid":53295,"parentid":50766,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Reach Heaven#Through Violence]]"}}}]},"1458":{"pageid":1458,"ns":0,"title":"Vigilance","revisions":[{"revid":56340,"parentid":55994,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Vigilance\n| Image       = Purple-Vigilance.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Gain (8;12) {{KW|Block}}. <br>Enter {{KW|Calm}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Calm\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Calm}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Vigilance}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 8 (12 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and makes you enter the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Obtaining Vigilance ==\nThe [[Watcher]] starts the game with one copy of {{C|Vigilance}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards, but can be obtained in the {{E|Match and Keep}} Event. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When entering {{KW|Calm}} if you are not in {{KW|Calm}} yet, you will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Calm}} has certain effects:\n** Playing {{C|Inner Peace}} will draw cards.\n** {{BD|Like Water}} from {{C|Like Water}} will give {{KW|Block}} at the end of your turn.\n\n* When you exit {{KW|Calm}}, it has the additional effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}